<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Student Learning Assessment Report</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  th, td { padding: 8px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }
  th { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
  .header-title { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .subtitle { font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section-heading { font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .metadata p { margin: 2px 0; font-size: 10pt; }
  .two-column-layout { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .two-column-layout > div { width: 48%; }
</style>

<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #000;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  th, td {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 8px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  th {
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .header-title {
    font-size: 18pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .section-heading {
    font-size: 14pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }
  .sub-heading {
    font-size: 12pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .list-item {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .signature-block {
    margin-top: 50px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    <h1 class="header-title">MARYMOUNT UNIVERSITY</h1>
  </div>
  <h2 class="subtitle">STUDENT LEARNING ASSESSMENT REPORT, {{ report_year }}</h2>
  <div class="metadata" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>PROGRAM: <span data-field="program_name">{{ program_name }}</span></p>
    <p>SUBMITTED BY: <span data-field="submitter_name">{{ submitter_name }}</span></p>
    <p>DATE: {{ report_date }}</p>
  </div>

  <h3 class="section-heading">Executive Summary: Description of Assessment Process</h3>
  <p>List all of the program's learning outcomes, as of the assessment year's catalog: (regardless of whether or not they are being assessed this year)</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 15%;">CIDA Standard</th>
        <th style="width: 45%;">Learning Outcome</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Year of Last Assessment</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Assessed This Year (Y/Yes)</th>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Year of Next Planned Assessment</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in assessment_table %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="assessment_table[{{ loop.index0 }}].cida_standard">{{ item.cida_standard }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="assessment_table[{{ loop.index0 }}].learning_outcome">{{ item.learning_outcome }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="assessment_table[{{ loop.index0 }}].year_last_assessment">{{ item.year_last_assessment }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="assessment_table[{{ loop.index0 }}].assessed_this_year">{{ item.assessed_this_year }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="assessment_table[{{ loop.index0 }}].year_next_planned">{{ item.year_next_planned }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    <h1 class="header-title">MARYMOUNT UNIVERSITY</h1>
  </div>

  <h3 class="section-heading">Course Assessment</h3>
  <p>Provide a brief description of the assessment process used including how results are shared and discussed and strengths, challenges, and planned improvements to the process, providing evidence of a culture of continuous improvement based on assessment. If there is something that is impeding your ability to implement improvements, please comment on those issues (generally not more than two paragraphs, may use bullet points):</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">CIDA Standard 8 Design Process</h4>
  <p>The {{ program_name }} curriculum map identifies the following courses as the primary location for evidence of student achievement in this category.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_8_1">{{ course_assessment_8_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_8_2">{{ course_assessment_8_2 }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Student projects are often include healthcare, education, hospitality, and retail.</p>
  <p>Interior design faculty assessed the thesis project completed by each enrolled student. Data is aggregated across all sections to access student learning outcomes defined by the Interior Design program.</p>
  <p>Thesis committee members also assessed the projects during the final thesis defense using the department's thesis defense rubric.</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">Practice Studio II (ID-306)</h4>
  <p>This is a 3rd year design studio where students design individual and group projects. The project practice area focuses on workplace design.</p>
  <p>Interior design faculty assessed the projects completed by each enrolled student. Data is aggregated across all sections to access student learning outcomes defined by the Interior Design program.</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">Exit Survey</h4>
  <p>Students that completed ID-409 during the assessment year were provided an exit survey where they were asked to self-report their competence in this SLA.</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">CIDA Standard 9 Communication</h4>
  <p>The {{ program_name }} curriculum map identifies the following courses as the primary location for evidence of student achievement in this category.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_9_1">{{ course_assessment_9_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_9_2">{{ course_assessment_9_2 }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Interior design faculty assessed the projects completed by each enrolled student. Data is aggregated across all sections to access student learning outcomes defined by the Interior Design program.</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">CIDA Standard 10 History</h4>
  <p>The {{ program_name }} curriculum map identifies the following courses as the primary location for evidence of student achievement in this category.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_10_1">{{ course_assessment_10_1 }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Foundation Studio III (ID-204) is a 2nd year design studio where students design individual and group projects. The project practice area focuses on residential design.</p>
  <p>Interior design faculty assessed the projects completed by each enrolled student. Data is aggregated across all sections to access student learning outcomes defined by the Interior Design program.</p>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">Exit Survey – This SLA was unintentionally omitted from last year's exit survey which means there is no data to report on this standard.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    <h1 class="header-title">MARYMOUNT UNIVERSITY</h1>
  </div>

  <h3 class="section-heading">Course Assessment (continued)</h3>
  <p>The {{ program_name }} curriculum map identifies the following courses as the primary location for evidence of student achievement in this category.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_11_1">{{ course_assessment_11_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="course_assessment_11_2">{{ course_assessment_11_2 }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Interior design faculty assessed the projects completed by each enrolled student. Data is aggregated across all sections to access student learning outcomes defined by the Interior Design program.</p>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">Assessment strengths include sampling of student work across multiple courses in the curriculum. Because department learning outcomes should be evident in all upper level design studios, the assessment process has the potential to indicate student achievement across the program.</h4>

  <h4 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 30px;">Assessment challenges include:</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>CIDA standards include multiple substandard that are specific competencies under the umbrella standard. While faculty looked specifically at sub-standards when evaluating SLAs, the exit survey only assesses the umbrella standard.</li>
    <li>Under the current assessment model where faculty assess student achievement within their courses, an undue burden falls on faculty teaching ID-409 and other upper level courses. Beginning in Fall 2019, the department is piloting a department-wide evaluation protocol that will collect assessment data from a majority of full-time faculty for each course under course assessment.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

